{"name":"Demure","hex":"#e8d4d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"demure","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Modest, quiet, reserved, or serious.","Affectedly modest, decorous, or serious; making a show of gravity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To look demurely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demure"}],"entries":[{"title":"Modesty","blocks":[{"text":"Modesty, sometimes known as demureness, is a mode of dress and deportment which intends to avoid the encouraging of sexual attraction in others. The word modesty comes from the Latin word modestus which means 'keeping within measure'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/CaliforniaBeachc1905.jpg/330px-CaliforniaBeachc1905.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modesty","wikidata":"Q11199149"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/1868-skirt-lengths-girl-ages-Harpers-Bazar.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f6/1868-skirt-lengths-girl-ages-Harpers-Bazar.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"1868 diagram from Harper's Bazaar showing proper girls' skirt lengths increasing as they grow up","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1868-skirt-lengths-girl-ages-Harpers-Bazar.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg/500px-Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg/1280px-Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg/500px-Orthodox_pilgrim.jpg?utm_source=en.